+## Short swipes, wider gutter and gentle release (2026-10-04)
+
+Requirements R01/V03/V04/V05/Q01. Owner still found navigation cumbersome and too prone to reverting, asked for a short gesture of a few centimetres to suffice, more empty space between visible pages, and smoother release especially when returning to the original page. This correction supersedes the 56-unit release threshold and fast-start easing above.
+
+Commitment now arms at **32 logical units**, rather than 56, and remains armed through slight backward finger relaxation. Only an actual drag back within **12 units** of the origin, crossing toward the opposite direction, cancellation, a second finger or a modal can revoke that direction. The latest displayed drag position determines the animation start; a noisy lift coordinate cannot undo commitment or teleport the pages. A deliberate return near the origin still cancels normally. Recognition and carousel/editor/slider/modal ownership remain unchanged.
+
+The gutter grows at half the finger displacement up to **64 logical units**. This leaves part of the next page visible from the first small movement, then opens a clearly wider empty strip on longer drags. Both directions preserve exact outgoing/incoming positions and spacing on commitment. Cancellation closes the gutter smoothly. Tab transitions use the full gutter too. Top navigation stays fixed and cached page controls remain reused.
+
+Completion now uses **sine ease-in/out over 180–320 ms**. Ordinary cancellation uses the same gentle start/end over **280–380 ms**, depending on the displayed travel. The original capped outer-edge spring remains. Release begins at the held position, with zero starting slope, rather than beginning with the return's maximum speed.
