+Initial graphical run had three failures (`TestScript-13788`): its early return sample was distorted by preceding PNG encoding/render-frame timing, and a compact-window assertion compared logical motion against physical image width. The second run retained one width assertion failure (`TestScript-23348`). Final tests compare against the actual initial logical position, and step the **real engine tween by 1/60 second** before resuming normal animation. Both release types must retain more than **97%** of their held distance after that first frame while still making progress; the previous fast-start easing would fail this bound. No runtime movement/ownership invariant was weakened.
